# SpendGate — OpenServ spending turnstile for Base AgentKit wallets

## Project Overview
SpendGate is an OpenServ agent that turns a human spending mandate (natural language) into a strict Base/USDC policy, then **allow / deny / escalate** every proposed spend before Coinbase AgentKit may move funds.
It does **not** custody user funds. Deterministic policy evaluation must never be replaced by LLM judgment.

**Hackathon:** SERV Hackathon Edition 01 · track **Coinbase AgentKit**  
**Repo:** https://github.com/aspekt19/SpendGate  
**Product name:** SpendGate (do not rebrand back to MandateGuard — that name collides with unrelated projects).

## Tech Stack
- Runtime: Node.js, TypeScript, ESM (`"type": "module"`)
- OpenServ: `@openserv-labs/sdk`, `@openserv-labs/client` (`provision`, `run`, `generate`, x402 triggers)
- Schemas: Zod
- Onchain executor: `@coinbase/agentkit` + CDP (`CdpEvmWalletProvider`), USDC on Base / Base Sepolia
- Local UI: Vite (vanilla TS) in `web/` → build output `web-dist/`
- Offline policy compile for UI: heuristic `src/policy/local-compile.ts` (production path uses OpenServ `compile_mandate`)

## Architecture (do not blur roles)

```
Human (owner) → SpendGate (OpenServ) → allow/deny/escalate → Spender (AgentKit) signs on Base
```

| Role | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| Human | Sets mandate; confirms escalations |
| SpendGate | Compile policy; deterministic gate; optional gated transfer |
| Spender | Proposes spends; may execute **only** after ALLOW |

## Project Structure
```
src/
  agent.ts                 # OpenServ agent + capabilities + provision/run
  policy/
    schema.ts              # MandatePolicy, SpendIntent, EvaluationResult (Zod)
    engine.ts              # Deterministic evaluateIntent / commitIntent / ledger
    local-compile.ts       # Offline NL→policy heuristics for UI only
  executor/
    gated-executor.ts      # evaluate → AgentKit transfer (or dry-run)
  store/
    fs-store.ts            # Persist policies/ledgers under data/
  demo/
    run-demo.ts            # CLI allow/deny/escalate scenarios
web/                       # Dialog UI (You / SpendGate / Spender)
web-dist/                  # Vite production build (Vercel output)
```

## Capabilities (OpenServ agent)
- `compile_mandate` — NL → MandatePolicy (via `this.generate` + Zod)
- `get_policy` — inspect policy + ledger + execute mode
- `evaluate_intent` — deterministic allow | deny | escalate (no tx)
- `execute_gated_transfer` — evaluate then AgentKit USDC transfer / dry-run
- `reset_ledger` — demo helper

## Chains & tokens
- Chain focus: **Base** (`base` / `base-sepolia` via `NETWORK_ID`)
- Currency in policy: **USDC only**
- USDC Base mainnet: `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913`
- USDC Base Sepolia: `0x036CbD53842c5426634e7929541eC2318f3dCF7e`
- Example allowlisted router (Uniswap Universal Router on Base): `0x3fC91A3afd70395Cd496C647d5a6CC9D4B2b7FAD`

## Environment
- Secrets only in `.env` — never commit `.env`, `.openserv.json`, CDP keys, or wallet private keys
- OpenServ: filled by `provision()` (`WALLET_PRIVATE_KEY`, `OPENSERV_API_KEY`, …)
- Optional deploy: `OPENSERV_USER_API_KEY`
- AgentKit live: `CDP_API_KEY_ID`, `CDP_API_KEY_SECRET`, `CDP_WALLET_SECRET`, `NETWORK_ID`
- Execute mode: `SPENDGATE_EXECUTE_MODE=dry-run|live` (default: live if CDP set, else dry-run)
- Legacy alias: `MANDATEGUARD_EXECUTE_MODE` still accepted in executor

## Scripts
- `npm run ui` — dialog UI (Vite)
- `npm run ui:build` — static build → `web-dist` (Vercel)
- `npm run demo` — offline CLI scenarios
- `npm run dev` — provision + run OpenServ agent
- `npm run typecheck` — `tsc --noEmit`

## Coding Rules
- Prefer ESM imports with `.js` extensions in compiled TS sources under `src/`
- Policy **decisions** live in `engine.ts` — pure, deterministic, no LLM
- LLM only for: mandate compilation helpers, explanations, OpenServ task routing
- Do not add custody, private-key handling in the UI, or blind auto-approve paths
- Keep components/files focused; match existing style; minimal diffs
- Do not invent on-chain spend vaults unless explicitly requested (roadmap item)
- Avoid renaming product to MandateGuard

## LLM workflow

Behavioral rules to reduce over-engineering and unclear edits. Prefer caution over speculative speed.

### 1. Think before coding
- State assumptions; if uncertain, ask.
- If multiple interpretations exist, present them — do not pick silently.
- Prefer the simpler approach; push back when warranted.

### 2. Simplicity first
- Minimum code that solves the request; nothing speculative.
- No features or abstractions beyond what was asked.
- If a change balloons, simplify before shipping.

### 3. Surgical changes
- Touch only what you must; do not “improve” adjacent code.
- Match existing style; do not refactor unrelated areas.
- Every changed line should trace to the user request.

### 4. Goal-driven execution
- Prefer verifiable outcomes (`npm run demo`, `npm run ui:build`, typecheck).
- For multi-step work, short plan + verify per step.

## Product positioning (for docs / pitches)
- **Not** “first spending-limit product in the world”
- **Yes** “OpenServ-native turnstile for AgentKit wallets on Base”: NL → policy → gate → optional execute
- Competitors may share the problem space (signed mandates, MCP guards); differentiate on SERV + AgentKit + dialog UX

## Frozen / out of scope (unless asked)
- Building a new marketplace or Ideaboard clone
- Robinhood Chain / brokerage MCP (possible later; not v1)
- Full Uniswap swap routing in executor (v1: evaluate swaps; execute transfer / x402_pay)
